Strategy: The client/context chooses a behavior/algorithm, usually because it wants a different way of doing something.

State: The object's internal state changes, and that state determines which behavior it exhibits.

| Pattern              | Core essence                                                     |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |                 |
| **Observer**         | Notify dependent objects when subject state changes              |
| **Command**          | Turn a request/action into an object                             |
| **Iterator**         | Separate traversal from collection implementation                |
| **State**            | Encapsulate behavior that changes according to an object's state |


